#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Einführung {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bits, gates, and circuits are the basic building blocks of quantum computing. You will learn quantum computation with the circuit model using quantum bits and gates, and also review the superposition, measurement, and entanglement.\n"
msgstr "Bits, Gates und Schaltkreise sind die grundlegenden Bausteine des Quantencomputings. Du wirst Quantenberechnung mit dem Schaltkreismodell unter Verwendung von Quantenbits und Gates erlernen und außerdem Superposition, Messung und Verschränkung wiederholen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson you will learn:\n"
"- Single-qubit gates\n"
"- Bloch sphere\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Measurement\n"
"- Two-qubit gates and entanglement state\n"
msgstr ""
"In dieser Lektion lernst du:\n"
"- Einzelne Qubit-Gates\n"
"- Bloch-Kugel\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Messung\n"
"- Zwei-Qubit-Gates und verschränkte Zustände\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the end of this lecture, you will learn about circuit depth, which is essential for utility-scale quantum computing.\n"
msgstr "Am Ende dieser Vorlesung wirst du etwas über die Schaltkreistiefe lernen, die für Quantencomputing im Utility-Scale-Bereich entscheidend ist.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Computation as a diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"
msgstr "2. Berechnung als Diagramm {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using qubits or bits, we need to manipulate them in order to turn the inputs we have into the outputs we need. For the simplest programs with very few bits, it is useful to represent this process in a diagram known as a *circuit diagram*.\n"
msgstr "Wenn wir Qubits oder Bits verwenden, müssen wir sie manipulieren, um die vorhandenen Eingaben in die benötigten Ausgaben umzuwandeln. Für die einfachsten Programme mit sehr wenigen Bits ist es nützlich, diesen Prozess in einem Diagramm darzustellen, das als *Schaltkreisdiagramm* bekannt ist.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bottom-left figure is an example of a classical circuit, and the bottom-right figure is an example of a quantum circuit. In both cases, the inputs are on the left and the outputs are on the right, while the operations are represented by symbols. The symbols used for the operations are called “gates”, mostly for historical reasons.\n"
msgstr "Die Abbildung unten links zeigt ein Beispiel eines klassischen Schaltkreises, und die Abbildung unten rechts zeigt ein Beispiel eines Quantenschaltkreises. In beiden Fällen befinden sich die Eingaben links und die Ausgaben rechts, während die Operationen durch Symbole dargestellt werden. Die für die Operationen verwendeten Symbole werden hauptsächlich aus historischen Gründen als „Gates\" bezeichnet.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"
msgstr "![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Single-qubit quantum gate {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"
msgstr "3. Einzelnes Qubit-Gate {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Quantum state and Bloch sphere {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"
msgstr "3.1 Quantenzustand und Bloch-Kugel {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit's state is represented as a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. An arbitrary quantum state is represented as\n"
msgstr "Der Zustand eines Qubits wird als Superposition von $|0\\rangle$ und $|1\\rangle$ dargestellt. Ein beliebiger Quantenzustand wird geschrieben als\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are complex numbers such that $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"
msgstr "wobei $\\alpha$ und $\\beta$ komplexe Zahlen sind, sodass $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ are vectors in the two-dimensional complex vector space:\n"
msgstr "$|0\\rangle$ und $|1\\rangle$ sind Vektoren im zweidimensionalen komplexen Vektorraum:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, an arbitrary quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Daher wird ein beliebiger Quantenzustand auch dargestellt als\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From this, we can see that the state of a quantum bit is a unit vector in a two-dimensional complex inner product space with an orthonormal basis of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. It is normalized to 1.\n"
msgstr "Daraus können wir erkennen, dass der Zustand eines Quantenbits ein Einheitsvektor in einem zweidimensionalen komplexen Innenproduktraum mit einer orthonormalen Basis aus $|0\\rangle$ und $|1\\rangle$ ist. Er ist auf 1 normiert.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ is also called the statevector.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin\\{pmatrix\\}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end\\{pmatrix\\}$ wird auch als Zustandsvektor (Statevector) bezeichnet.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Ein einzelner Qubit-Quantenzustand wird auch dargestellt als\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\theta$ and $\\varphi$ are the angles of the Bloch sphere in the following figure.\n"
msgstr "wobei $\\theta$ und $\\varphi$ die Winkel der Bloch-Kugel in der folgenden Abbildung sind.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"In the next few code cells, we will build up basic calculations from constituent pieces in Qiskit. We'll construct an empty circuit and then add quantum operations, discussing the gates and visualizing their effects as we go.\n"
"You can run the cell by \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Import the libraries first.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"In den nächsten Code-Zellen werden wir grundlegende Berechnungen aus den Bestandteilen in Qiskit aufbauen. Wir konstruieren einen leeren Schaltkreis und fügen dann Quantenoperationen hinzu, wobei wir die Gates besprechen und ihre Auswirkungen visualisieren.\n"
"Du kannst die Zelle mit „Shift\" + „Enter\" ausführen. Importiere zuerst die Bibliotheken.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the quantum circuit {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Vorbereitung des Quantenschaltkreises {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will create and draw a single-qubit circuit.\n"
msgstr "Wir erstellen und zeichnen einen Einzelqubit-Schaltkreis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "X gate {#x-gate}"
msgstr "X-Gate {#x-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The X gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around the $x$ axis of the Bloch sphere.\n"
"Applying the X gate to $|0\\rangle$ results in $|1\\rangle$, and applying the X gate to $|1\\rangle$ results in $|0\\rangle$, so it is an operation similar to the classical NOT gate, and is also known as bit flip. The matrix representation of the X gate is below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Das X-Gate ist eine $\\pi$-Rotation um die $x$-Achse der Bloch-Kugel.\n"
"Die Anwendung des X-Gates auf $|0\\rangle$ ergibt $|1\\rangle$, und die Anwendung des X-Gates auf $|1\\rangle$ ergibt $|0\\rangle$, sodass es eine Operation ähnlich dem klassischen NOT-Gate ist und auch als Bit-Flip bekannt ist. Die Matrixdarstellung des X-Gates ist unten gezeigt.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In IBM Quantum&reg;, the initial state is set to $|0\\rangle$, so the quantum circuit above in matrix representation is\n"
msgstr "Bei IBM Quantum&reg; ist der Anfangszustand auf $|0\\rangle$ gesetzt, sodass der obige Quantenschaltkreis in Matrixdarstellung lautet\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's run this circuit using a statevector simulator.\n"
msgstr "Als Nächstes führen wir diesen Schaltkreis mit einem Zustandsvektor-Simulator aus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vertical vector is displayed as row vector, with complex numbers (the imaginary part is indexed by $j$ ).\n"
msgstr "Der vertikale Vektor wird als Zeilenvektor angezeigt, mit komplexen Zahlen (der Imaginärteil wird durch $j$ indiziert).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "H gate {#h-gate}"
msgstr "H-Gate {#h-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hadamard gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around an axis halfway between the $x$ and $z$ axes on the Bloch sphere. Applying the H gate to $|0\\rangle$ creates a superposition state such as $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. The matrix representation of the H gate is below.\n"
msgstr "Das Hadamard-Gate ist eine $\\pi$-Rotation um eine Achse auf halbem Weg zwischen der $x$- und $z$-Achse auf der Bloch-Kugel. Die Anwendung des H-Gates auf $|0\\rangle$ erzeugt einen Superpositionszustand wie $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. Die Matrixdarstellung des H-Gates ist unten gezeigt.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Das ist\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This superposition state is so common and important, that it is given its own symbol:\n"
msgstr "Dieser Superpositionszustand ist so häufig und wichtig, dass er sein eigenes Symbol hat:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By applying the $H$ gate on the $|0\\rangle$, we created a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ where measurement in the computational basis (along z in the Bloch sphere picture) would give you each state with equal probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Durch Anwendung des $H$-Gates auf den $|0\\rangle$ haben wir eine Superposition aus $|0\\rangle$ und $|1\\rangle$ erzeugt, bei der eine Messung in der Rechenbasis (entlang z im Bloch-Kugel-Bild) jeden Zustand mit gleicher Wahrscheinlichkeit ergibt.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|-\\rangle$ state {#rangle-state}"
msgstr "$|-\\rangle$-Zustand {#rangle-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might have guessed that there is a corresponding  $|-\\rangle$ state:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"To create this state, first apply an X gate to make $|1\\rangle$, then apply an H gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Du hast vielleicht vermutet, dass es einen entsprechenden $|-\\rangle$-Zustand gibt:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Um diesen Zustand zu erzeugen, wende zuerst ein X-Gate an, um $|1\\rangle$ zu erhalten, und dann ein H-Gate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b8e96fc4-6708-415e-b8fc-ac69eaeae750-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b8e96fc4-6708-415e-b8fc-ac69eaeae750-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/f42b82aa-7a15-4f81-8530-b997d4c6e0de-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/f42b82aa-7a15-4f81-8530-b997d4c6e0de-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is\n"
msgstr "Das ist\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H|1\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\\\n"
"-1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\\\n"
"-0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle) = |-\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H|1\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\\\n"
"-1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\\\n"
"-0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle) = |-\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the $H$ gate on $|1\\rangle$ results in an equal superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, but the sign of $|1\\rangle$ is negative.\n"
msgstr "Die Anwendung des $H$-Gates auf $|1\\rangle$ ergibt eine gleichmäßige Superposition aus $|0\\rangle$ und $|1\\rangle$, aber das Vorzeichen von $|1\\rangle$ ist negativ.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Single-qubit quantum state and unitary evolution {#32-single-qubit-quantum-state-and-unitary-evolution}"
msgstr "3.2 Einzelner Qubit-Quantenzustand und unitäre Evolution {#32-single-qubit-quantum-state-and-unitary-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The actions of all the gates we have seen so far have been *unitary*, which means they can be represented by a unitary operator. In other words, the output state can be obtained by acting on the initial state with a unitary matrix:\n"
msgstr "Die Wirkungen aller Gates, die wir bisher gesehen haben, waren *unitär*, was bedeutet, dass sie durch einen unitären Operator dargestellt werden können. Mit anderen Worten, der Ausgabezustand kann durch Anwendung einer unitären Matrix auf den Anfangszustand erhalten werden:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{'}\\rangle = U|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{'}\\rangle = U|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A unitary matrix is a matrix satisfying\n"
msgstr "Eine unitäre Matrix ist eine Matrix, die folgende Bedingung erfüllt\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger}U =U U^{\\dagger} = I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger}U =U U^{\\dagger} = I.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In terms of quantum computer operation, we would say that applying a quantum gate to the qubit evolves the quantum state. Common single-qubit gates include the following.\n"
msgstr "In Bezug auf den Betrieb von Quantencomputern würden wir sagen, dass die Anwendung eines Quanten-Gates auf das Qubit den Quantenzustand entwickelt. Häufige Einzelqubit-Gates umfassen die folgenden.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli gates:\n"
msgstr "Pauli-Gates:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 1|+|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 1|+|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\\n"
"i & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -i|0\\rangle \\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\\n"
"i & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -i|0\\rangle \\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 0|-|1\\rangle \\langle 1|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 0|-|1\\rangle \\langle 1|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the outer product was calculated as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"wobei das äußere Produkt wie folgt berechnet wurde:\n"
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Other typical single-qubit gates:\n"
"$$\n"
"H= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n"
"S = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & i \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"T = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & exp(i\\pi/4) \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Weitere typische Einzelqubit-Gates:\n"
"$$\n"
"H= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n"
"S = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & i \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"T = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & exp(i\\pi/4) \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta X/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}X = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  -i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"-i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta X/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}X = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  -i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"-i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Y/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Y = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  - sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Y/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Y = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  - sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_z(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Z/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"e^{-i\\theta /2} &  0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta /2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_z(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Z/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"e^{-i\\theta /2} &  0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta /2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The meaning and use of these are described in more detail in the [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) course.\n"
msgstr "Die Bedeutung und Verwendung dieser Gates wird im Kurs [Grundlagen der Quanteninformation](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) detaillierter beschrieben.\n"

